      {
        "kind": "kpis",
        "summary": "",
        "status": "inferred",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "A useful conditional KPI is delivery efficiency (for example, cost per engaged reach or per conversion) for ad groups where interests are selected versus ad groups where interests are left broad, because the mechanism is defined as delivering to people with higher interaction with the chosen interests — so performance differences may plausibly follow from the targeting, but this is an inference, not a documented uplift figure.",
            "status": "inferred",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "source_id": "tiktok.paid_social.targeting",
                "source_url": "https://ads.tiktok.com/resources/help/article/ad-targeting?lang=en",
                "locator": "**Interests:** Deliver to people based on their higher interaction with certain interests. For example, gaming.",
                "source_site": "TikTok Ads Help Center",
                "source_title": "Ad targeting",
                "raw_sha256": null,
                "cleaned_sha256": null
              }
            ],
            "conditions": [
              "Observed differences in delivery efficiency by interest selection are correlative and may also reflect creative, bidding or smart-targeting expansion effects"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Any reporting of whether ads actually served within the selected interest audience should account for smart targeting, which by design can deliver outside your designated audience settings.",
